## Why This Is Asked

This question tests depth in CAPA design for cross-tenant data exposure caused by policy migration bugs in a real-time data mesh. It evaluates the ability to model evidence, define a region-aware lifecycle, implement a minimal API, and build measurable containment strategies plus RCA artifacts and canary rollouts.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model capturing evidence, tenant IDs, policy metadata, dashboards, and timestamps
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine for CAPA progression
- RBAC/policy migration risks in real-time data platforms
- Minimal REST API design to link logs/traces to CAPA records
- Canary rollout and region-validated testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal CAPA creation endpoint
app.post('/api/capa', async (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, tenants, dashboards, policyHash, evidence } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA, link logs/traces, trigger workflow
  res.status(201).send({ id: incidentId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate cross-tenant exposure detection at scale across regions?
- What data retention and privacy considerations would you encode in the CAPA API?

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design a beginner-level CAPA process for shared resources and governance, rather than implementing quick fixes alone.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Evidence-rich REST API
- Operational metrics
- RCA templates and canary remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express API scaffolding for /caps
const express = require('express')
const app = express()
app.use(express.json())
let caps = []

app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = { id: Date.now().toString(), ...req.body }
  caps.push(cap)
  res.status(201).json(cap)
})

app.get('/caps', (req, res) => {
  res.json(caps)
})

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('CAPA service running'))
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a privacy-risk incident into a concrete CAPA with measurable outcomes, suitable for beginner-level roles at scale.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model design
- Lifecycle/state machine modeling
- Minimal REST API for CAPA CRUD with evidence
- Practical privacy metrics and verification
- RCA templating and canary-based remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoint to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
const caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const c = {
    id: `CAPA-${caps.length+1}`,
    title: req.body.title,
    rootCause: req.body.rootCause,
    containment: req.body.containment,
    correctiveAction: req.body.correctiveAction,
    preventiveAction: req.body.preventiveAction,
    evidence: req.body.evidence || [],
    status: 'discovered',
    owner: req.body.owner || 'unassigned',
    createdAt: new Date(),
    updatedAt: new Date()
  };
  caps.push(c);
  res.status(201).json(c);
});
app.listen(3000, () => console.log('CAPA API listening'));
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce evidence integrity in the API layer?
- What monitoring would you add to ensure canary remediation succeeds before full rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests end-to-end CAPA design for data-label drift impacting model training with region-specific effects, governance signals, and remediation validation.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, lineage, owners
- Region-aware lifecycle: detect → contain → remediate → verify; per-region SLAs
- REST API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Region metrics: containment MTTR, drift recurrence, false-positive drift alerts
- RCA template and canary rollout plan for labeling changes

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  region: string;
  evidence: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owners: string[];
  status: "detect" | "contain" | "remediate" | "verify";
  slaHours: number;
  policyLinks?: string[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with existing labeling pipelines and drift detectors, and what alerts would you surface?
- How would you test the CAPA program in a staging environment with synthetic drift scenarios and ensure safe canaries?

